{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF8fUpb8JJZvbNGQEmji","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"prompt\": \"A square, full-bleed nonrepresentational abstract painting that fills the entire canvas edge to edge, with no frame, wall, room, or gallery setting. No recognizable objects, figures, faces, bodies, scenes, landscapes, horizons, machines, diagrams, symbols, icons, letters, numbers, or text. Palette: deep indigo and near-black ground, threaded through with cadmium orange, pale bone white, and a cold teal that flickers at the edges. Composition: a dense, layered field where many thin translucent strata overlap and push against one another, with a few heavy, sweeping gestures cutting diagonally across the surface. Brushwork varies sharply: some areas are scraped thin with a palette knife to reveal the ground beneath, others are loaded with thick impasto ridges that catch light. Texture is rough and tactile, with dry-brush drag marks, drips that stop short, and pockets of fine, scratched hatching. Contrast is strong where the orange meets the indigo, and softer where the teal dissolves into white. Spatial tension comes from a crowded upper-left quadrant opening into a broad, quiet expanse of empty space in the lower right, where a single restrained stroke hangs unresolved. Rhythm is irregular, with pulses of dense marks followed by sudden pauses. The overall feeling is one of restless searching held in tension with stillness, rendered purely through color, gesture, and material.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_tokens":16579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":470},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"paren